===Etymology===
{{bor|en|xno|-}} and {{bor|en|frm|oyez|notext=1}}, {{m|fro|oiez}}, imperative plural of {{m|fro|oir||to hear}}, from {{der|en|fro|oïr||to hear}}, itself from {{der|en|la|audiō|audiō, audīre|to hear}} ({{m|en|oyez}} in particular corresponding to the second-person plural imperative form, {{m|la|audite}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈəʊˌjeɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/oʊˈjeɪ/|lang=en}}<!--homophonous with "oh yay!"-->
* {{hyphenation|o|yez|lang=en}}
{{rfap||UK|lang=en}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# [[hear ye|Hear ye]]. Attend. (Called by public [[crier]]s or in [[court]] usually three times to secure silence).

====Usage notes====
* It is still used in the United States Supreme Court, and in many state supreme courts, though some lower courts have dropped its use.

